- op: discuss  # d83c
  at: '2026-11-01T02:26:27Z'  # d83c
  by: agent  # d83c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d83c
  clock: 4  # d83c
  nonce: d83c  # d83c
  message: "Fixed in PR #1983 (e0e236386c on dev). Root cause: the caller was fetched by bare name from a run-wide registry (last file wins), and the walk carried the outermost function name into nested functions. Now the WI-kosar mechanism: the enclosing symbol by position (symbols_at over file_symbols), the callee from this file first, full name before short name. The same family was fixed in apex, hack, smithy and prisma. Live repro on merged dev: hypergumbo survey on a.luau/b.luau each with local function helper(): rc=0, b.luau:5 beta() comes from b.luau:4-6:helper and b.luau:10 beta() from b.luau:9-11:inner (before: from a.luau helper, and from outer). Tests in test_luau/apex/hack/smithy/prisma. Corpus litellm prisma: cross-file edges 27 to 0. Residual filed: WI-gikuk (java extends/implements source by package-less name)."  # d83c
